\title{Quaternion and order-three subgroups}

\tag{notes}
\tag{math}
\tag{fgap}
\tag{group-action}
\tag{quaternion}
\tag{hurwitz}

\p{We now separate two small groups inside the nonzero quaternions. The first
is the quaternion group generated by #{i} and #{j}. The second is generated
by the Hurwitz unit #{\omega}. Conjugation by #{\omega} then tells us how the
second group acts on the first.}

\p{This is the concrete input for a later construction of the binary
tetrahedral group. We stop before that construction here: the present notes
only define the two factors and calculate their action.}

